      "description": "One-loop three-point function $I_3^D(\\nu_1, \\nu_2, \\nu_3; Q_1^2, 0, 0, M_1^2, M_2^2, 0)$ with two massive internal lines (masses $M_1, M_2$), one massless internal line, one off-shell external leg of virtuality $Q_1^2$ and two on-shell massless external legs. Evaluated with unit propagator powers ($\\nu_i = 1$) in $D = 4 - 2\\varepsilon$. Expressed as sum of a Kampe de Feriet $S_1$ function and a Horn $H_2$ function (region IIIb representation), epsilon-expanded using MultiHypExp to obtain series coefficients as multiple polylogarithms / classical $\\operatorname{Li}_{1,1}$. Used to validate agreement between the IIIb and IIb analytic continuations of Anastasiou-Ellis-Gehrmann-Melrose.",
